============================================================
STAGE 1
============================================================
Generating stage 1 environment...
  Rationale: Stage 0 achieved 98% success with the cube at exact center (zero randomization, fixed rotation). Now we introduce moderate positional randomization: the cube spawns uniformly in [-0.05, 0.05] on both x and y axes, which is wider than the default Lift task's [-0.03, 0.03]. We also enable random rotation. This forces the policy to generalize its reach-grasp-lift behavior across different cube positions rather than memorizing a single trajectory.

The reward shaping structure is preserved but with slightly reduced bonus magnitudes (proximity 0.2 vs 0.3, grasp 0.4 vs 0.5, lift 0.8 vs 1.0, success 1.5 vs 2.0) to begin weaning the policy off heavy scaffolding while still providing enough signal for the new generalization challenge.

Since the agent already has a solid grasp-and-lift policy and just needs to adapt to position variation within a small region, ~150 policy updates should suffice, but we budget 200 updates as a conservative upper bound with early stopping.
  Timesteps: 6,348,800
